[b]Speculative Markets 1.1: everything since 1.0[/b]

[b]Competing Exchanges[/b]
[list]
[*]Exchanges now compete. Each has contest slots: one, plus one per Standing above Provincial, up to four. The slots sit at the top of the new Competition section, with the Exchanges contesting you beside them.
[*]Start a contest from the compete button on the Leading Exchanges list, or right-click a country on the map. Stop Competing works the same way.
[*]Contesting needs at least Engaged interest in the strategic region of their capital. You cannot contest an Exchange that already contests you. Contesting adds involvement in that region at once and every month.
[*]Each competitor costs 25 to 150 influence a month by its Standing. Contesting costs 10 relations at once, then 1 a month down to Poor. A new contest cannot be ended in its first year.
[*]A contest is a tug of war settled after 5 years. The bar starts from the two scores and each action that works pushes it 10%, up to 5 pushes a side. Within 20% of the middle it is a draw. A win takes trust from the loser. Past 75% a decisive win takes twice as much, plus part of the loser's investment pool income for a year.
[*]Each contest past the first spreads you thinner, lowering your score in all of them.
[*]Ending a contest early settles it as a loss where the bar stands. The other Exchange gains as if it had won.
[*]Five competitor actions, each once a year per target: Bear Raid, Lure Their Capital, Press Campaign, Hold the Line and Shore Up. Costs and effects scale with the size of both Exchanges.
[*]When a competitor acts against you, an event lets you answer in kind, shore up or keep calm.
[*]AI Exchanges pick contests they can win, act more as a contest nears its end, hold the line against your pushes, and cut their losses before a decisive defeat.
[*]Capital fleeing a Financial Panic goes first to a competing Exchange. Bear Raids show in the Market Confidence breakdown.
[*]Competition section: Competitor Actions on Us, Our Competitors and Competing With Us, each with a contest bar you can hover for what every result would do.
[/list]

[b]Exchange score, Trust and World Centres[/b]
[list]
[*]The Exchange score grows more slowly with sheer size, so more great powers can compete.
[*]The top three Exchanges are World Centres: cheaper loans, more influence, smaller losses from foreign panics and one competitor free of upkeep.
[*]The score and the four Standings show as one block, each Standing card filling as your score climbs through it.
[*]Trust has its own bar with its four levels, Distrusted to Trusted, named above it. Hover a level to see what it does. Trust is a new concept.
[/list]

[b]Paths to Renown[/b]
[list]
[*]Three new paths: Futures Pit, Lender to Nations and Railway Mania, each with a painted icon.
[*]Every path has a drawback that grows with your place, and pulls levers in other systems.
[*]Home of Great Companies now scores Company Strength.
[*]Deep Pockets gives a smaller investment pool bonus.
[/list]

[b]Blue Chips[/b]
[list]
[*]A company at 70 or more prosperity for 12 months becomes a blue chip. Blue chips soften crashes and foreign panics, add trust, raise Capitalist investment, cut loan interest and pull your contests your way. Up to 10 count.
[*]Events when a company becomes a blue chip or starts slipping. Each year the most prosperous is Company of the Year.
[*]A Blue Chips strip and status tags on the Companies rows of the Speculation tab. New concepts: Blue Chip and Company Strength.
[/list]

[b]Speculation and Banking[/b]
[list]
[*]A Speculative Excess bar, and a fifth risk for the bubble.
[*]A Lending Standards scale, and a bar showing what a panic would take from your investment pool.
[*]A panic takes less of the investment pool at low leverage.
[/list]

[b]Interface and text[/b]
[list]
[*]Finance tabs renamed Trading Floor, Speculation, Banking and Exchanges.
[*]Tooltips rewritten in vanilla's style, shorter and with concept icons. Rank icon on the Exchanges list.
[*]Translated into all 10 languages.
[/list]

[b]Fixes in 1.1[/b]
[list]
[*]A Great Issue or its cooldown could stay forever after loading a save.
[*]Revolutionary journal entries were not inherited correctly.
[*]A script error when hovering the button to stop pursuing an Exchange name.
[/list]

[b]1.0.1 to 1.0.6[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed a crash showing Correction, Bust and Collapse notifications.
[*]Fixed the Open Finance buttons in the Financial Markets journal entry and goods panel.
[*]Fixed duplicate Financial Markets journal entries in older saves, and journal labels disagreeing with Finance.
[*]Fixed tied contests showing an old result, outdated loan tooltips, overstated confidence losses at zero, and missing penalties after surrendering a war.
[*]Fixed duplicate rival notifications and AI rescue chances not matching their rates.
[*]Closed markets now clear relief, depression effects and Exchange bonuses. Bank rescues no longer shorten a fresh panic.
[*]Many fixes for annexed, merged and missing countries in rankings, rivals and Exchange seats.
[*]Opening another panel closes Finance. Panic tooltips show the national penalties.
[/list]
